    "created_at": "2023-09-01T13:47:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-01T13:47:13Z",
    "body": "I suspect these `add` and `remove` methods predate the DOM (and having an in-memory tree representation of all the elements in the HTML), and come from the era when the things you could do from javascript were limited to forms, images, frames, and a few other things.  It's not clear to me whether they're worth extending to other things or whether they exist only for backwards-compatibility.",
